@startuml
title Damage pipeline — where weakness and modifiers combine

skinparam linetype ortho

/'
  DealDamage names only an amount and a target, so weakness, ReduceDamage and
  IncreaseDamage had nowhere to meet, and IDurationEffect's `duration` had
  nowhere to be stored. Both are fixed here.
'/

class DamageEvent <<record>> {
    - source: Optional<PokemonInPlay>
    - target: PokemonInPlay
    - baseAmount: int
    /' False for spread/bench damage and for between-turns poison and burn,
       which skip weakness and most modifiers. '/
    - isAttackDamage: boolean
}

class DamageCalculator {
    + resolve(DamageEvent, ResolutionContext): int
}

/'
  Installed on PokemonInPlay by an IDurationEffect and expired between turns.
  This is the storage that IDurationEffect previously lacked.
'/
class ActiveModifier <<record>> {
    - kind: ModifierKind
    - amount: int
    - expiresOnTurn: int
}

enum ModifierKind {
    INCREASE_DAMAGE_DEALT
    REDUCE_DAMAGE_TAKEN
    PREVENT_DAMAGE
}

DamageCalculator ..> DamageEvent
DamageCalculator ..> ActiveModifier
ActiveModifier o-- ModifierKind
PokemonInPlay *-- ActiveModifier

@enduml

@startuml
title Damage pipeline — order of application

start
:base = DealDamage.damageAmount.evaluate(ctx);

if (isAttackDamage?) then (yes)
  :+ INCREASE_DAMAGE_DEALT modifiers on the **source**;
  if (defender weak to attacker's type?) then (yes)
    :+ weaknessDamage (Pocket: +20);
  endif
  :- REDUCE_DAMAGE_TAKEN modifiers on the **target**;
  if (PREVENT_DAMAGE on target?) then (yes)
    :damage = 0;
  endif
else (no — spread / bench / poison / burn)
  :no weakness, no modifiers;
endif

:clamp to >= 0;
:target.damage += amount;
:dispatch DamageDealt;
:Battle.checkKnockouts();

stop

note right
  Order matters and is not commutative: weakness applies to the
  already-increased base, and reduction is subtracted after
  weakness. Getting this wrong is silently wrong — it only shows
  up on cards that stack two of the three.

  Weakness applies only to the ATTACKED ACTIVE. Bench damage,
  spread damage and between-turns status damage all bypass it,
  which is why isAttackDamage is on the event rather than being
  inferred from whether a source exists.
end note

@enduml
